                            	  3852: FormatHeartsInTextBuf:
                            	  3853:     ; [$0E]: hearts value
                            	  3854:     ; [$0F]: heart partial
                            	  3855:     ; Y: The offset of first character in buffer
                            	  3856:     ;
                            	  3857:     ; The end of the bottom row is $12 bytes after the
                            	  3858:     ; start of the top row. We're writing to two transfer
                            	  3859:     ; records. We write the top row in the first transfer
                            	  3860:     ; record wherever the caller chooses. The second
                            	  3861:     ; transfer record has to begin with the heart tiles.
                            	  3862:     ; So, 7 (offset to end of first row) + 3 (size of transfer
                            	  3863:     ; header) + 8 (length of bottom row) = 18 ($12).
                            	  3864:     ;
