                            	  1879:     ; We'll get a 0 or 1 depending on the direction of the door.
                            	  1880:     ;
                            	  1881:     ; If the attribute of the door is "open", "key", or "key 2";
                            	  1882:     ; then you have shorter distance to cover. So use the
                            	  1883:     ; previous value as is to use indexes 0 and 1.
                            	  1884:     ;
                            	  1885:     ; Otherwise, add 2 to use indexes 2 and 3 to walk farther
                            	  1886:     ; to get out of the way of the wall or door.
